{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607304-i-need-feedback-on-a-new-face-for-the-sabbat","id":607304,"title":"I Need Feedback on a New Face for the Sabbat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-29T18:14:32-07:00","id":607304,"title":"I Need Feedback on a New Face for the Sabbat","content":"I started playing the World of Darkness games with Vampire in college in the 90s, so I admit to having some love for the Old Canon as well as the New. There is a lot to be said for bits of all of it. Recently, my weekly group asked me to run a WoD game. The group is a mix of experienced and inexperience gamers; both with respect to gaming in general and the WoD specifically. I know I want to do a game that pays homage to the original while bringing in the wonderful elements of the Requiem.<br /> <br /> Long story short, I am starting the PCs as Unbound in New York under the rule of the re-imagined Sabbat. From there, they will be drawn into an effort by a coalition of other Covenants \u2013who have chosen to call themselves the Camarilla in homage to the ancient body- who seek to dethrone the Sabbat and claim the city for themselves. Once that plays out, nature will follow suit as the Camarilla collapses under the weight of infighting and self interest. All in all, it should leave the PCs with ample opportunity to impact the face of the city.<br /> But before I can get there, I need to re-imagine the Sabbat. What follows is my first draft of just that. I would love to see constructive feedback. Thanks for reading!<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Sabbat of New York</b></u><br /> The Sanguineous Catechism\u2019s first chapter states unequivocally the theological position of the Sanctified; the Original Sin of Adam and Eve taints every man, woman and child and leaves them incapable of being inherently \u201cgood\u201d; the stain of that sin condemns them to separation from God; this world is the physical form of that separation, a prison for the Sons of Adam and the Daughters of Eve. Humanity\u2019s only hope lies in the Grace of God present in the Blood of Christ, shed by the spear of Longinus. <br /> <br /> Prior to their Embrace, the vampire is no more or less eternally Damned than any other human soul. However, the Embrace, the blood of the Kindred- wholly isolates the new vampire from God\u2019s Grace; the Blood of Caine is wholly incompatible with the Blood of Christ. Not because of any weakness in God\u2019s ability to provide Grace to the repentant, but because of the nature of God\u2019s plan; created by God, the Kindred have been set among humanity as wolves in order that Christ\u2019s Sheep might better learn the nature of their dependence on Grace.<br /> <br /> To the Kindred of the Sabbat, a faction of the Lancea et Sanctum, the role of Kindred as tormentors of humanity is paramount to their Requiems. Comprised of some of the most zealous of the followers of Longinus, the members of the Sabbat are devoted to the doctrinal split known as the Heresy of Milan. Named for the Council of Milan, at which the heresy was first debated by the Sanctified, at its heart, the heresy teaches that God, who is always faithful, would never forget His love for any soul and that even the Embrace is not without its opportunity for Grace. Further, the Kindred are not the Damned of God but rather the very Elect of God; that they have been chosen to serve the highest of purposes and that those who serve well can earn their redemption, a place in Paradise. The Kindred of the Sabbat believe that God offers salvation to the Kindred through the zeal with which they fill their roles as wolves among the sheep. <br /> <br /> While the Sabbat rejects the central authority of the Sanctified leadership, they recognize the wisdom of Longinus\u2019 teaching and organize into independent, local bodies called Consistories that rarely govern more than a single domain and operate independently of each other. The Consistory of New York, the largest such body in the world, is comprises of five Assemblages; each of which governs one of the city\u2019s five boroughs and is traditionally comprised of no fewer than seven members (seven being the Judaic number of perfection) or more than twelve (twelve being the number of the priesthood). A sixth body, the Plurality, is lead by a Teaching Elder who is served by six Ruling Elders. Together these seven Kindred represent the leadership of the covenant in the city.<br /> <br /> The Consistory of New York is careful to prevent any other covenant, including the mainline Lancea et Sanctum, from becoming either to numerous or to entrenched within the city. To this end, the Plurality routinely organizes \u201cRevivals\u201d among the Assemblages with each Assemblage providing a designated \u201cevangelist\u201d. Together with two of the Ruling Elders, the evangelists crusade through the city to thin the ranks of competing covenants and the Unbound alike. Those who find themselves confronted by a Sabbat Revival are given two choices, convert or die.<br /> <br /> <b>Assemblages of the Consistory of New York</b><br /> <br /> <u>The Plurality</u><br /> The senior leadership of the Sabbat in New York, the Plurality is ostensibly the unbiased arbiter of disputes between the Assemblages. In truth, the Teaching Elder, a Ventrue Elder who claims to be the famous minister Cotton Mather, is a master manipulator who plays the five Assemblages against one another to ensure that his power remains unchallenged. The six Ruling Elders serve Mather, five of them acting as advisors \u2013and secret police- among the Assemblages with the sixth being Mather\u2019s personal assistant.<br /> <br /> For reasons as yet not fully understood by any of the city\u2019s Kindred, Mather has recently launched a crusade against the werewolves of the city. The Plurality has ordered the wholesale embrace of expendable soldiers whose blood he has been shedding wantonly in the pursuit of an agenda that can only be defined as the purge of werewolves from the domain of the Consistory.<br /> <br /> <u>The Broken Seal</u><br /> Comprised almost entirely of Ventrue stock, the Broken Seal controls Manhattan. Their leadership has openly challenged Cotton Mather\u2019s decisions regarding the war with the werewolves and is rumored to be seeking to displace Mather for the good of the Consistory and the preservation of the secrecy which best serves their role as the monsters in the darkness. If they could be certain that another Ventrue would secure the position of Teaching Elder, they would have long ago backed the Repentant Few in their challenge of Mather\u2019s leadership. Their position is further complicated by the discovery of a Kindred faction in Manhattan of which the Broken Seal was aware prior to the start of the Conflict; a growing presence in Chinatown.<br /> <br /> <u>The First Trumpet</u><br /> Also known as Rate-7, or r8-7, an allusion to Revelations 8:7 from which they drew their Assemblage\u2019s name, the First Trumpet governs Brooklyn and has endured the brunt of the bloodshed in Mather\u2019s Crusade. Looking to the verse of their inspiration, the Sabbat of the First Trumpet have reveled in the destruction, seeing the destruction of the werewolves as in line with the destruction of the green places alluded to in the biblical passage. The war has taken a toll on the Assemblage, however, attrition has left them with the thinnest blood and youngest leadership.<br /> <br /> <u>The Repentant Few</u><br /> The Repentant Few governs Queens and is the most independent of the five Assemblages, often finding reasons to delay compliance with a request from the Plurality and on at least one occasion allowing a Ruling Elder to become \u201clost\u201d for several weeks while in their care. They have contributed the least to Mather\u2019s War, proclaiming it as a waste of Kindred unlives that in no way serves God\u2019s purpose for them. They maintain that it is a violation of the Sabbat\u2019s deeply held theology in that it in no way serves to bring humanity closer to God; a position that has begun to spread through the Consistory. <br /> <br /> <u>The Tenth Crown</u><br /> Controlling the Bronx, the Sabbat of the Tenth Crown have gone to great lengths to ensure instability and conflict on the streets of that borough; few areas of the city are more dangerous than the Bronx. Murder, rape, assault; the violence native to the domain of the Tenth Crown serves to attract the worst of humanity and provide the Assemblage with the greatest opportunity to serve God\u2019s purpose. Mather\u2019s War has afforded the Assemblage with yet another source of fuel for the violence they have cultivated. Or at least that\u2019s the official story. In truth, the Assemblage is comprised entirely of Kindred of Belial\u2019s Brood. The Infernalists infiltrated the Assemblage decades ago and since that time have converted or killed off every member of it. The violence of the Bronx serves some purpose, but to be certain it is not the purpose of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <u>Milites Interfecti Agnus</u><br /> This order of militant novices serves as the shock troops of the Consistory of New York both within the city and outside its borders. Comprised only of female Kindred, the Assemblage controls Staten Island, which it polices militantly. It is said that when God needs a killing, He sends an angel. When the Consistory needs a killing, they send the Soldiers of the Slaughter Lamb. As the warriors of the Consistory, it chafes at the Soldiers that they have not been allowed a more direct role in the conflict with the werewolves. They see the position of the Repentant Few as cowardly; openly criticizing the other Assemblage afraid to face the werewolves, preferring to challenge only sheep.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7085-dissenterknight","name":"DissenterKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T19:54:15-07:00","id":607382,"title":"","content":"I really like this. I run a Masquiem game, and I think this mash-up makes a lot of sense. A couple questions, do you have any history on your Sabbat? Do you include the Salubri in your Sabbat? (sorry, favorite Clan. &gt;.&lt;) and, can I pick it apart for my personal Masquiem Sabbat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T00:00:38-07:00","id":607533,"title":"","content":"Personaly, I would make this Sabbat a little more like the original one. Instead of a Lancea et Sanctum heresy, they could be a Covenant of their own with a complex mythology based on the Book of Nod (that could be an actual book, like the Testament of Longinus is), including the legend of Caine and of the first and second cities.<br /> <br /> In a Requiem game, those Cainites with differentiate from the Sanctified for a focus on a Old Testament-like mythos, instead of something based on the New Testament. Their origin could even be jewish, even if today most of them where christians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T10:45:41-07:00","id":608186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607304-i-need-feedback-on-a-new-face-for-the-sabbat?p=607533#post607533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personaly, I would make this Sabbat a little more like the original one. Instead of a Lancea et Sanctum heresy, they could be a Covenant of their own with a complex mythology based on the Book of Nod (that could be an actual book, like the Testament of Longinus is), including the legend of Caine and of the first and second cities.<br /> <br /> In a Requiem game, those Cainites with differentiate from the Sanctified for a focus on a Old Testament-like mythos, instead of something based on the New Testament. Their origin could even be jewish, even if today most of them where christians.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I considered making them a stand alone covenant, still am as I plan. But I was worried about covenant overload. The idea of the Sabbat as Jewish to the LeS as Christian is appealing. Though there would be a need to rewrite the existing theology of the reimagined Sabbat as it is very New Testament. As a minister and a student of church history, I think the idea of division within the Sanctified is very appealing to me from a art reflects life point if view. <br /> <br /> I do think I missed the mark re: the blood drenched nature of the original version. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7085-dissenterknight","name":"DissenterKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T10:58:55-07:00","id":608203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607304-i-need-feedback-on-a-new-face-for-the-sabbat?p=607382#post607382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this. I run a Masquiem game, and I think this mash-up makes a lot of sense. A couple questions, do you have any history on your Sabbat? Do you include the Salubri in your Sabbat? (sorry, favorite Clan. &gt;.&lt;) and, can I pick it apart for my personal Masquiem Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have not yet develop a history bbeyond the nod to Milan. No plan to use Salubri or any sort of antitribue, though I am going to Cappadoceans up my sleeve as a &quot;next threat&quot; if the group taskes the story that way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7085-dissenterknight","name":"DissenterKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T11:57:14-07:00","id":608265,"title":"","content":"I don't think a sixth covenant would be a problem, or in fact that you even need to use all five covenants there. Except as far away presences that grant some support to the few members on the city (maybe just the PCs and a few more). Your idea already puts this group as central to the setting, to make them an independent covenant will only improve the experience.<br /> <br /> This kind of theocracy don't mix nor repel three of the Covenants. In that regard, you can have Ordo Dracul, Carthians and Invictus as common presence in the city, living with the official religion, or completely absent, without appeal for local Kindred nor interest on the city. Thinking about Sabbat, I would make your NY home to Ordo Dracul with actual authorization and encouragement to do their experiments (maybe with a cabbalistic approach) and a chapter of the Carthian Movement with ideas similar to the cWoD first Anarch Revolt. Invictus wouldn't appeal to local Kindred or be outright forbidden by the local &quot;state&quot;.<br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone and Lancea et Sanctum have the most interest in dealing with this religious calamity, but theirs would be a strange alliance. But again, odd alliances where as much a part of old Camarilla. The most effective banner against said theocracy would still be Invictus, but they could send only one or two powerful representatives to be behind the others. Lancea and Ordo strike a peace to work against this threat, but don't want to risk actual members and need a less religous face to gather allies, so they ally with some Ordo that doesn't want to work within the stablishment of the city and join with strange foreign help, a Mage of the Tremere Legacy. All the whyle, the Carthian Movement do want to have a say in the affairs and stablishes a chapter to be involved and if possible take over when all is done, an Anarch Movement inside this Camarilla arguing against Invictus leadership.<br /> <br /> Most of the actual &quot;rebels&quot; and Camarilla members are just Unbound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T12:08:59-07:00","id":608288,"title":"","content":"I like where you're going, so much in fact that I am stealing pieces of it! <br /> <br /> The chronicle idea is to open with the Sabbat in charge, move through an open war, then finish with the revolution after the revolution; that always being the one that reshapes the landscape in surprising ways. I have plans for the Ordo and there is no reason that they cannot be in the city already. Further, I see a similar status to the Carthiuan/ Invuctus situation; in my model the Carthiuan are struggling to hold the Camarilla council together while the Invuctus sabotage them and go to great lengths to make it clear that the dream can not last.<br /> <br /> Though it was nice of the Carthians to shed so much blood for the cause...<br /> <br /> Making the Sabbat a covenant would be as easy as declaring a schism at Milan, rather than a mere heresy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7085-dissenterknight","name":"DissenterKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T12:35:24-07:00","id":608339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607304-i-need-feedback-on-a-new-face-for-the-sabbat?p=607533#post607533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personaly, I would make this Sabbat a little more like the original one. Instead of a Lancea et Sanctum heresy, they could be a Covenant of their own with a complex mythology based on the Book of Nod (that could be an actual book, like the Testament of Longinus is), including the legend of Caine and of the first and second cities.<br /> <br /> In a Requiem game, those Cainites with differentiate from the Sanctified for a focus on a Old Testament-like mythos, instead of something based on the New Testament. Their origin could even be jewish, even if today most of them where christians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering there is a cainite heresy based on Cain as first vampire in the Requiem for Rome books, porting at least some noddist lore should not be too hard, though in some aspects it might parallel Akhud mythic origins in VII, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T17:36:16-07:00","id":608650,"title":"","content":"OK, I took a second stab at the Sabbat as a stand alone covenant; stepped back and added in some history to boot. Decided to build it on the Cappadocians and Assamites. As before, I'd love your feedback!<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Sabbat of New York </u></b><br /> <b>The Council of Diospolis</b><br /> In December of 415, the church fathers of Christianity gathered at Diospolis, present day Laodicea in Turkey. On their agenda was the trial of Pelagius, a British-born ascetic moralist well known throughout ancient Rome. The theologian stood accused of heresy for his position regarding predestination and the free will of humanity; maintaining that humanity did not need divine aid in the performance of good works. Further, citing Deuteronomy 24:16 in support of his position, Pelagius denied that humanity was \u201cwounded by Adam\u2019s sin\u201d; teaching that humanity was able to satisfy the Law of God in their own strength. <br /> <br /> In the course of the council, Pelagius and the doctrine that bore his name were examined and confronted by the bishop of C\u00e6sarea. From its shadows, Kindred of the Lancea et Sanctum watched the proceedings; themselves deeply divided over the nature of free will and the growing popularity of the Cappadocian Doctrine and its author, Japheth of Derinkuyu, among the Sanctified. Deeply influenced by the writings of the theologian Caelestius, a student of Pelagius, Japheth\u2019s teachings relied on the concept of Original Sin in conjunction with Pelagius\u2019 thoughts on Free Will. By the end of the Council of Diospolis, Pelagius had recanted his theology and denounced Caelestius and, unknowingly, Japheth as well. <br /> <br /> Undeterred by Pelagius\u2019 recanting, on returning to Derinkuyu in Cappadocia, Japheth codified his doctrine and gathered a core of believers, twelve in number. Together with his devoted acolytes, he spent the long nights teaching from the Testament of Longinus and the letters of Caelestius. He taught that the Original Sin of Adam and Eve taints every man, woman and child and leaves them incapable of being inherently \u201cgood\u201d and that the stain of that sin condemns humanity to separation from God. Further, this world is the physical form of that separation, a prison for the Sons of Adam and the Daughters of Eve. It\u2019s at this point that Japheth\u2019s teachings diverge from those of the Lancea Sanctum. As Caelestius taught that humanity was challenged to grow into the image of Christ through good works done in their own strength; Japheth taught the Kindred to could find salvation in through works; the works they were called to perform, the works of wolves among sheep. Each act of terror, each torment, each moment of wanton bloodletting was a step closer to Paradise for the Kindred performing them. <br /> <br /> <b>The Founding of a Covenant</b><br /> With the coming of the Passover in 416, Japheth called his disciples to a ritual deep beneath Derinkuyu. There they found the bishop of Diospolis stripped, bound and suspended from the ceiling. When his disciples were seated, Japheth rose, took a silver chalice to the bishop and opened the churchman\u2019s femoral artery, collecting his blood in the chalice. Then, he mixed his own along with a measure of that of each of his disciples and all drank. As they did, Japheth repeated the tenants of his doctrine, point by point declaring first of the new covenant\u2019s laws and traditions. In this way both the Blood Feast and the Sabbat were formed.<br /> <br /> Over the next year Japheth and his disciples worked to convert the remainder of the Cappadocian Kindred to their covenant. They tolerated no other covenants to function within their domain; giving all who they encountered the choice between faith and fire. Once the Sabbat had an established power base they expanded outwardly into the rest of the Anatolian Peninsula, establishing Assemblages in the cities they came to and seeking out Lancea et Sanctum parishes, which they sought to disrupt or destroy.<br /> <br /> As the covenant expanded west, they reached the small market town of Pazark\u00f6y, where they encountered a secretive clan of Kindred who hotly resisted their advanced. Their first interactions were violent and resulted in the death of several Sabbat. It was only when Japheth journeyed to Pazark\u00f6y and asked to speak with the leader of the sect that common ground could be found and the bloodshed ended. Led to an ancient fortress south of the market, Japheth learned of the Assamites and they learned of the Sabbat and the Covenant\u2019s view of the Requiem.<br /> <br /> Since that time the Cappadocians have functioned as the scholars and theologians of the Sabbat cells with the Assamites functioning as the warriors, assassins, advisors and mystics. It is rare to see members of either clan within any other covenant. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7085-dissenterknight","name":"DissenterKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}